<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The pre-first-frame window background for API 28-30, which have no SplashScreen API.

    A layer-list rather than a plain colour so those versions still get the mark rather than a
    black rectangle: crateBlack ground, disc centred and held to a fixed size so it matches the
    scale the platform splash uses on 31+.

    **Do not wrap the disc in `<bitmap>`.** It was written that way and it crashed the app on
    launch — every device below API 31, every release from 0.2 to 0.4.1 — with

        XmlPullParserException: <bitmap> requires a valid 'src' attribute

    `<bitmap>` decodes a raster; `ic_splash_mark` is a VectorDrawable, and handing one to
    `android:src` is not a fallback that degrades, it is an inflation failure. It surfaces as
    `Resources$NotFoundException` on `windowBackground`, which the framework resolves inside
    `PhoneWindow.generateLayout` before `onCreate` returns, so the process dies before a single
    line of this app's code runs.

    Nothing caught it because `values-v31/themes.xml` overrides `windowBackground` with the real
    SplashScreen API, so API 31+ never inflates this file — and every device it had been run on
    was API 31+. Found on an API 28 emulator.

    A layer-list `<item>` takes a vector directly and has carried `android:width`/`android:height`
    since API 23, which is below the floor, so the size is set here rather than by wrapping.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:drawable="@color/crate_black" />
    <item
        android:drawable="@drawable/ic_splash_mark"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:width="160dp"
        android:height="160dp" />
</layer-list>
